{"doe":{"w":"doe","zh":["母鹿","麀","雌鹿"],"ipa":{"uk":"/dəʊ/","us":"/doʊ/"},"ety":[{"n":1,"chain":[{"l":"enm","f":"do","t":"inh","g":"(female) fallow deer"},{"l":"ang","f":"dā","t":"inh"},{"l":"gmw-pro","f":"*daihā","t":"inh","g":"female deer, mother deer"},{"l":"ine-pro","f":"*dʰeh₁(y)-","t":"der","g":"to suck (milk), to suckle"}],"text":"From Middle English do (“(female) fallow deer”), from Old English dā, from Proto-West Germanic *daihā (“female deer, mother deer”), from Proto-Indo-European *dʰeh₁(y)- (“to suck (milk), to suckle”). Cognate with Middle Scots da, dae (“female fallow deer”), Danish då (“fallow deer”), Sanskrit धेनु (dhenú, “cow, milk-cow”), Old English dēon (“to suckle”), Old English delu (“teat”). Related also to female, filial, fetus.","cog":[{"l":"gmw-msc","f":"da"},{"l":"da","f":"då"},{"l":"sa","f":"धेनु","tr":"dhenú"},{"l":"ang","f":"dēon"},{"l":"ang","f":"delu"}]}],"pos":[{"p":"noun","e":0,"senses":[{"d":"A female deer; also used of similar animals such as antelope (less commonly a goat, as nanny is also used).","tags":["countable","uncountable"],"ex":["A doe from round a spruce stood looking at them\nAcross the wall, as near the wall as they.\nShe saw them in their field, they her in hers."],"syn":["hind"],"grp":0,"zh":"母鹿；麀；雌鹿"},{"d":"A female fallow deer.","tags":["countable","uncountable"],"grp":2},{"d":"A female rabbit or hare.","tags":["countable","uncountable"],"grp":3},{"d":"A female squirrel.","tags":["countable","uncountable"],"grp":5},{"d":"A female kangaroo.","tags":["countable","uncountable"],"syn":["blue flyer"],"grp":0,"zh":"母鹿；麀；雌鹿"}],"forms":[["pl","does"]]}],"grp":[{"label":"female deer","zh":["母鹿","麀","雌鹿"],"p":"noun","e":0,"tr":{"fr":["fr:biche"],"it":["it:cerva"],"es":["es:cierva"],"pt":["pt:corça"]}},{"label":"female roe deer","zh":[],"p":"noun","e":0,"tr":{"fr":["fr:chevrette"],"it":[],"es":[],"pt":[]}},{"label":"female fallow deer","zh":[],"p":"noun","e":0,"tr":{"fr":["fr:daine"],"it":["it:daina"],"es":[],"pt":[]}},{"label